":"EX-0009.02","d3f:definition":"At the OS layer the attacker targets primitives that schedule work and mediate hardware. Maintenance builds may expose shells or management consoles; misconfigurations around these interfaces can provide paths to command interpreters or privileged syscalls. Exploitation yields kernel-mode execution, arbitrary memory read/write, or control of scheduling and address spaces, letting the actor tamper with FSW processes, intercept command paths, or manipulate storage and bus drivers beneath application checks. The technique leverages generic OS weaknesses adapted to the spacecraft’s particular build, turning low-level control into mission-facing effects that appear to originate from legitimate processes.","d3f:modifies":{"@id":"d3f:OperatingSystem"},"rdfs:label":"Operating System - SPARTA","rdfs:seeAlso":{"@id":"https://sparta.aerospace.org/technique/EX-0009/02/"},"rdfs:subClassOf":{"@id":"d3f:EX-0009"},"skos:prefLabel":"Operating System"}]},"subtechniques":{"@context":{"rdfs":"http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#","owl":"http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#","d3f":"http://d3fend.mitre.org/ontologies/d3fend.owl#","skos":"http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"},"@graph":[{"@id":"d3f:EX-0009","d3f:attack-id":["EX-0009"],"d3f:top-level":["true"],"rdfs:hasSubClass":[{"@id":"d3f:EX-0009.03"},{"@id":"d3f:EX-0009.01"},{"@id":"d3f:EX-0009.02"}],"rdfs:label":["Exploit Code Flaws - SPARTA"],"skos:prefLabel":["Exploit Code Flaws"]},{"@id":"d3f:EX-0009.01","d3f:attack-id":["EX-0009.01"],"rdfs:label":["Flight Software - SPARTA"],"rdfs:subClassOf":[{"@id":"d3f:EX-0009"}],"skos:prefLabel":["Flight Software"]},{"@id":"d3f:EX-0009.02","d3f:attack-id":["EX-0009.02"],"rdfs:label":["Operating System - SPARTA"],"rdfs:subClassOf":[{"@id":"d3f:EX-0009"}],"skos:prefLabel":["Operating System"]},{"@id":"d3f:EX-0009.03","d3f:attack-id":["EX-0009.03"],"rdfs:label":["Known Vulnerability (COTS/FOSS) - SPARTA"],"rdfs:subClassOf":[{"@id":"d3f:EX-0009"}],"skos:prefLabel":["Kno